KEY: ORG
SUMMARY: Set the address for the following output
BODY:
ORG expression

SETS THE ADDRESS WHERE SUBSEQUENT ASSEMBLED BYTES
ARE PLACED. MULTIPLE ORG REGIONS ARE ALLOWED ONLY
IN INCREASING ADDRESS ORDER; GAPS BETWEEN THEM ARE
ZERO-FILLED IN THE RAW OUTPUT. MOVING BACKWARD
OVER ALREADY-WRITTEN OUTPUT IS AN ERROR.

  ORG $8000
---
KEY: EQU
ALIASES: EQ
SUMMARY: Define a named constant
BODY:
NAME EQU expression
NAME EQ expression   (SAME DIRECTIVE, SHORT FORM)

MUST BE RESOLVABLE WHEN THE ASSEMBLER REACHES IT,
SO DEFINE CONSTANTS BEFORE THEY ARE USED. ORDINARY
INSTRUCTION AND DATA OPERANDS MAY STILL REFER TO
LABELS DEFINED LATER IN THE FILE.

  SCREEN   EQU   $2000
  COUNT    EQU   16
---
KEY: DS
SUMMARY: Reserve and zero-fill a number of bytes
BODY:
DS expression

RESERVES expression BYTES OF RAW OUTPUT, ALL SET
TO ZERO, STARTING AT THE CURRENT ADDRESS.
---
KEY: DFB
ALIASES: DB, BYTE
SUMMARY: Emit comma-separated bytes or strings
BODY:
DFB value, value, ...
DB value, value, ...      (SAME DIRECTIVE)
BYTE value, value, ...    (SAME DIRECTIVE)

EACH value IS AN 8-BIT EXPRESSION OR A QUOTED
STRING; STRINGS EMIT ONE BYTE PER CHARACTER.

  MESSAGE  ASC   "HELLO"
           DFB   0
---
KEY: DW
ALIASES: DA, WORD
SUMMARY: Emit comma-separated 16-bit values
BODY:
DW value, value, ...
DA value, value, ...      (SAME DIRECTIVE)
WORD value, value, ...    (SAME DIRECTIVE)

EACH value IS A 16-BIT EXPRESSION, EMITTED LOW
BYTE FIRST (LITTLE-ENDIAN), MATCHING HOW THE 6502
READS ADDRESS OPERANDS AND VECTORS.

  DW SCREEN, SCREEN+40
---
KEY: ASC
ALIASES: TEXT
SUMMARY: Emit a quoted ASCII string or byte values
BODY:
ASC "text"
TEXT "text"       (SAME DIRECTIVE)

EMITS ONE BYTE PER CHARACTER OF A QUOTED STRING.
CAN ALSO TAKE COMMA-SEPARATED BYTE EXPRESSIONS THE
SAME WAY DFB DOES.
---
KEY: HEX
SUMMARY: Emit hexadecimal byte pairs
BODY:
HEX byte byte ...

EACH byte IS A TWO-DIGIT HEXADECIMAL PAIR. SPACES
OR COMMAS ARE BOTH ACCEPTED AS SEPARATORS. USEFUL
FOR EMITTING A SPECIFIC OPCODE BYTE WHEN AN
UNDOCUMENTED INSTRUCTION HAS MORE THAN ONE ENCODING
FOR THE SAME SYNTAX (SEE THE JAM OR ANC CARDS).
---
KEY: PUT
ALIASES: USE, INCLUDE
SUMMARY: Assemble another source file at this point
BODY:
PUT path
USE path          (SAME DIRECTIVE)
INCLUDE path       (SAME DIRECTIVE)

INSERTS path'S SOURCE AT THIS LOCATION, AS IF IT
WERE TYPED INLINE. path USES ORDINARY FANTICON
CONSOLE PATHS. INCLUDES MAY NEST UP TO 16 LEVELS.
---
KEY: END
SUMMARY: Mark the logical end of source
BODY:
END

MARKS THE LOGICAL END OF THE SOURCE FILE. ANYTHING
AFTER IT IS NOT ASSEMBLED.
---
KEY: MAC
SUMMARY: Begin a named or positional macro definition
BODY:
NAME MAC value;dest=$20
  ...body using ]VALUE and ]DEST...
EOM

PLACE THE MACRO'S NAME IN THE LABEL FIELD AND MAC
IN THE OPERATION FIELD. OPTIONAL NAMED PARAMETERS
FOLLOW MAC, SEPARATED BY ; OR ,. TRAILING PARAMETERS
MAY HAVE DEFAULTS. @LOCAL LABELS ARE UNIQUE TO EACH
EXPANSION. DEFINITIONS WITHOUT A PARAMETER LIST KEEP
THE LEGACY ]1 THROUGH ]8 POSITIONAL FORM.

  LOADIMM  MAC VALUE;DEST=$20
           LDA   #]VALUE
           STA   ]DEST
           EOM
---
KEY: EOM
ALIASES: <<<
SUMMARY: End a macro definition (see MAC)
BODY:
EOM
<<<               (SAME DIRECTIVE)

CLOSES A MAC DEFINITION. SEE THE MAC CARD FOR THE
FULL PATTERN.
---
KEY: PMC
ALIASES: >>>
SUMMARY: Invoke a macro by name
BODY:
PMC name;arg1;arg2;...
>>> name;arg1;arg2;...    (SAME DIRECTIVE)

INVOKES A MACRO DEFINED WITH MAC, SUBSTITUTING
ARGUMENTS FOR NAMED PARAMETERS AND ]1, ]2, ETC. THE
MACRO'S NAME MAY
ALSO BE USED DIRECTLY IN THE OPERATION FIELD, LIKE
AN ORDINARY MNEMONIC. EXPANSION MAY NEST UP TO 32
LEVELS. PMC IS RECOMMENDED FOR ; ARGUMENTS SO THE
EDITOR CANNOT MISTAKE THEM FOR COMMENTS.

  PMC LOADIMM;$42;$20
---
KEY: DO
ALIASES: IF
SUMMARY: Begin a compile-time conditional block
BODY:
DO expression
IF expression          (SAME DIRECTIVE)
  ...included when expression is nonzero...
ELSE
  ...included when expression is zero...
FIN / ENDIF

THE EXPRESSION MAY USE EARLIER EQU CONSTANTS AND THE
FULL INTEGER EXPRESSION SYNTAX, INCLUDING ==, !=, <,
>, <=, AND >=. CONDITIONAL BLOCKS MAY NEST.
---
KEY: ELSE
SUMMARY: Merlin conditional-assembly directive
BODY:
SELECTS THE OTHER BRANCH OF A DO/IF BLOCK. EACH BLOCK
MAY CONTAIN AT MOST ONE ELSE. SEE THE DO CARD.
---
KEY: FIN
ALIASES: ENDIF
SUMMARY: End a compile-time conditional block
BODY:
FIN
ENDIF                 (SAME DIRECTIVE)

CLOSES A DO OR IF BLOCK. SEE THE DO CARD.
---
KEY: LUP
ALIASES: REPEAT
SUMMARY: Begin a compile-time repeat block
BODY:
LUP count;INDEX
REPEAT count;INDEX     (SAME DIRECTIVE)
  ...body using ]INDEX or ]#...
--^ / ENDREP

EXPANDS THE BODY COUNT TIMES. ]INDEX IS THE ZERO-BASED
ITERATION NUMBER; ]# IS ITS SHORT ALIAS. BLOCKS MAY
NEST. COUNT MUST RESOLVE WHEN ENCOUNTERED AND BE FROM
0 THROUGH 65535.
---
KEY: --^
ALIASES: ENDREP
SUMMARY: End a compile-time repeat block
BODY:
--^
ENDREP                (SAME DIRECTIVE)

CLOSES A LUP OR REPEAT BLOCK. SEE THE LUP CARD.
---
KEY: DUM
SUMMARY: Begin a symbol-only data layout
BODY:
NAME DUM origin
FIELD DS size
...
DEND

DEFINES FIELD OFFSETS WITHOUT EMITTING BYTES. A NAMED
LAYOUT PREFIXES FIELDS AS NAME.FIELD AND DEFINES
NAME.SIZE AT DEND. OMIT NAME FOR GLOBAL DUMMY LABELS.
ENTRIES MAY BE LABELED DS, EQU, OR EQ DIRECTIVES.
---
KEY: DEND
SUMMARY: Close a DUM dummy section (see DUM)
BODY:
DEND

CLOSES A DUM SYMBOL-ONLY LAYOUT. SEE THE DUM CARD.
---
KEY: PROC
SUMMARY: Begin a procedure-local label scope
BODY:
NAME PROC
.LOOP  ...
       BNE .LOOP
       RTS
ENDPROC

DEFINES NAME AS THE ENTRY LABEL. DOT-PREFIXED LABELS
INSIDE BECOME NAME.LABEL. PROC ADDS NO REGISTER SAVES,
STACK FRAME, OR RTS, AND PROCEDURES CANNOT NEST.
---
KEY: ENDPROC
SUMMARY: End a procedure-local label scope
BODY:
ENDPROC

CLOSES THE CURRENT PROC SCOPE. SEE THE PROC CARD.
---
KEY: XC
SUMMARY: Merlin CPU-mode toggle directive
BODY:
NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.

MERLIN USES XC TO TOGGLE 65C02/65816 OPCODE
SUPPORT. FANTICON'S ASSEMBLER TARGETS THE NMOS
6502 ONLY, SO THIS IS RECOGNIZED BY SYNTAX
COLORING FOR SOURCE COMPATIBILITY BUT DOES NOT DO
ANYTHING.
---
KEY: MX
SUMMARY: Merlin register-width directive (65816)
BODY:
NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.

APPLIES TO THE 65816'S VARIABLE-WIDTH A/X/Y
REGISTERS, WHICH FANTICON'S NMOS 6502 DOES NOT
HAVE. RECOGNIZED BY SYNTAX COLORING ONLY.
---
